#    on any other iteration, so it is safe to run this loop in
#    parallel. This will be lowered to an OpenMP parallel-for.
init_s_loop = kernel_bicg.find_loop("j")
kernel_bicg = parallelize_loop(kernel_bicg, init_s_loop)

# 2. Tile the inner j-loop of the main BiCG computation.
#
#    After the transformation, the main loop body looks conceptually like:
#
#      for i in 0..n:
#        ri = r[i]
#        qi = 0
#        for jo in 0..ceil(m / TILE_J):
#          for ji in 0..TILE_J:
#            j = jo*TILE_J + ji
